  "description": "T1. Red Oak. Laterally reduce away from the main carriage way by 2m laterally on the lower crown to eliminate the bus hitting the tree. Above this, laterally reduce two lateral branches to match the lower crown shape. Laterally reduce by 2m, two lower sections that protrude towards the gate at Eastcote close.\r\rT2. False Acacia. Laterally reduce to give 2m clearance of the adjacent telephone lines to prevent future problems.\r\rT3. English Oak. Laterally reduce to give 3m clearance of the neighbouring building to prevent future contact. Crown lift one pendular branch that over hangs the lawn up to 4m from ground level.",
